---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Show a run's metadata: id, status, timestamps, launcher, and description.

Max Compute Hours and Setup Timeout are the values that the launch requested,
when the run has them. One compute hour is one core running for one hour.
Elapsed is wall-clock time, which also spans provisioning, setup and teardown.
Source is the `antithesis.source` the run was launched from, when the launcher
recorded one. The run also has its user-defined attributes
(`--param attrs.<name>=<value>` at launch) and the `vcs.*` parameters that the
Antithesis GitHub trigger action records (repository, branch, and commit), under
Attributes and Version Control.

An incomplete run also has its failure moment (Failure Hash/VTime), to pass to
`runs logs`, and a failure reason when the run reports one. Use --web to open
the triage report in a browser.

Examples:
  snouty runs show <run_id>
  snouty runs show <run_id> --web

Add --json for machine-readable output. The run prints as one JSON object. With
--web it prints the report URL as {"url": ...} and opens no browser:
  snouty --json runs show <run_id> | jq -r .status

Usage: snouty runs show [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

Options:
  -w, --web
          Open the run's triage report in a browser instead of printing details

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
